---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SeaBreak from '../../components/SeaBreak.astro';
import { celestial, scenes } from '../../config/images';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CTABand from '../../components/CTABand.astro';
const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Explore Astrology', href: '/explore/' },
  { label: 'Birth Chart Basics', href: '/explore/birth-chart-basics/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Birth Chart Basics. How a natal chart works"
  description="A birth chart is a map of the sky at your moment of birth. Learn what planets, signs, houses, angles, and aspects contribute, and why astrologers read them together."
  path="/explore/birth-chart-basics/"
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
  <section class="hero hero--split">
    <div class="container">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Start here</p>
        <h1>Birth chart basics</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Before learning what every symbol means, it helps to know what you are actually looking at.
          A birth chart is a map of a particular sky from a particular place and moment. Astrology
          begins with the interpretation of that map.
        </p>
      </div>
      <img class="hero__img" src={scenes.birthChartBasics.src} srcset={scenes.birthChartBasics.srcset} sizes="100vw" alt={scenes.birthChartBasics.alt} width={scenes.birthChartBasics.width} height={scenes.birthChartBasics.height} fetchpriority="high" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container basics-map">
      <div class="basics-map__visual" role="img" aria-label="Simplified teaching diagram showing the zodiac around a chart, houses inside it, the horizon and meridian crossing the wheel, planets placed within the chart, and aspect lines connecting planets">
        <div class="basics-map__zodiac">ZODIAC</div>
        <div class="basics-map__houses">HOUSES</div>
        <div class="basics-map__horizon"><span>HORIZON</span></div>
        <div class="basics-map__meridian"><span>MERIDIAN</span></div>
        <span class="basics-map__planet basics-map__planet--one" aria-hidden="true">☉</span>
        <span class="basics-map__planet basics-map__planet--two" aria-hidden="true">☽</span>
        <span class="basics-map__planet basics-map__planet--three" aria-hidden="true">♂</span>
        <svg class="basics-map__aspects" viewBox="0 0 300 300" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M92 87 L211 111 L145 221 Z" />
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="prose flow">
        <p class="eyebrow">Read the picture first</p>
        <h2>What the wheel is showing you</h2>
        <p>
          Imagine standing where you were born at the moment you were born and mapping the sky all
          around you, including the half below the horizon. The planetary positions, zodiac,
          horizon, and meridian can be calculated astronomically. Astrology begins when we interpret
          the relationships among those positions.
        </p>
        <dl class="factlist">
          <dt>Zodiac</dt><dd>The twelve signs form the reference band against which planetary positions are described.</dd>
          <dt>Houses</dt><dd>The chart is divided into areas of experience, anchored to the local place and time.</dd>
          <dt>Angles</dt><dd>The horizon and meridian create four important orientation points, including the Ascendant and Midheaven.</dd>
          <dt>Planets</dt><dd>The Sun, Moon, and planets occupy positions within that structure.</dd>
          <dt>Aspects</dt><dd>Angular relationships connect planets to one another and help show how separate functions interact.</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose flow" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-7);">
        <h2>Four useful questions make the chart easier to enter</h2>
        <p>These are teaching shortcuts, not a complete interpretation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid--4">
        <article class="card"><h3><a href="/explore/planets/">Planet</a></h3><p><strong>What is operating?</strong></p><p>A drive or function within the chart.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3><a href="/explore/signs/">Sign</a></h3><p><strong>How does it express?</strong></p><p>A style or mode through which a planet operates.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3><a href="/explore/houses/">House</a></h3><p><strong>Where does it show up?</strong></p><p>An area of experience where the symbolism may become visible.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3><a href="/explore/aspects/">Aspect</a></h3><p><strong>How do the parts relate?</strong></p><p>An angular relationship that connects planetary functions.</p></article>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: var(--space-6);"><a class="btn btn--primary" href="/tools/explore-your-chart/">Try these layers in the chart explorer</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SeaBreak image={celestial.galaxyTidepool} />

  <section class="section section--sea">
    <div class="container prose flow">
      <h2>Why your birth time matters</h2>
      <p>
        Birth time anchors the chart to the local horizon and meridian. It determines the rising
        sign, exact angles, and house structure, which is why two people born on the same date in
        the same city can share many planetary placements while having different chart orientations.
        If you do not know yours, <a href="/birth-time/">there are still useful ways to work with what is known</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Why one placement is never the whole person</h2>
      <p>
        Online astrology often makes one placement sound self-contained: “Mars in Aries means this”
        or “Moon in Pisces means that.” Those descriptions can teach vocabulary, but Mars is also in
        a house, making aspects, ruling other parts of the chart, and operating inside one particular
        life. The ingredients repeat across charts. The combinations do not.
      </p>

      <h2>What a chart is not</h2>
      <p>
        A chart is not a verdict, a personality prison, or a set of instructions. It offers another
        way to look at patterns, tensions, capacities, and timing. How those possibilities are lived
        depends on the person, the circumstances, and the choices made along the way.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABand
    heading="Now try reading the layers yourself."
    body="The chart explorer turns this map into a guided lesson: choose a planet, sign, and house, then see why synthesis matters more than isolated labels."
    buttonLabel="Open the Chart Explorer"
    buttonHref="/tools/explore-your-chart/"
    secondaryLabel="Continue to the Big Three"
    secondaryHref="/explore/the-big-three/"
  />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .basics-map {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    align-items: center;
  }
  .basics-map__visual {
    position: relative;
    width: min(82vw, 420px);
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    margin-inline: auto;
    border: 26px solid var(--color-teal-tint);
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-teal);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: radial-gradient(circle, var(--color-parchment) 0 45%, transparent 46%), var(--surface);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-1);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .basics-map__zodiac,
  .basics-map__houses {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .12em;
  }
  .basics-map__zodiac { top: 10px; color: var(--color-teal-deep); }
  .basics-map__houses { top: 72px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .basics-map__horizon,
  .basics-map__meridian { position: absolute; inset: 50% 4%; height: 1px; background: var(--color-clay); }
  .basics-map__horizon span { position: absolute; right: 0; top: 6px; font-size: .7rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .basics-map__meridian { transform: rotate(90deg); }
  .basics-map__meridian span { position: absolute; right: 0; top: 6px; font-size: .7rem; font-weight: 700; transform: rotate(-90deg); }
  .basics-map__planet { position: absolute; z-index: 2; font-size: 1.7rem; color: var(--color-navy); }
  .basics-map__planet--one { left: 21%; top: 20%; }
  .basics-map__planet--two { right: 18%; top: 31%; }
  .basics-map__planet--three { left: 43%; bottom: 18%; }
  .basics-map__aspects { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
  .basics-map__aspects path { fill: none; stroke: var(--color-gold); stroke-width: 2; opacity: .75; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .basics-map { grid-template-columns: .85fr 1.15fr; }
  }
</style>
